Pietro Massini
 wrote:

> Hi,

> anyone has succesfully installed a Turtle Beach Pinnacle?

> Please tell me what to do with the firmware files (pnddk100.zip),

> because I can't compile them, they are for DOS!

> 

> Pietro


Pietro,


I'm using a Fiji (i.e. Pinnacle without the onboard Kurzweil synth) and it works ok (unresolved problems with duplex though).


I think you need the 'conv' program to convert the firmware files; conv comes with the driver package downloaded from Andrew Veliath's website:

	http://atv.ne.mediaone.net/linux-multisound/


Once you've unpacked the tar file, read the directions in the file MultiSound. It tells you how to make 'conv' and use it to convert the DOS binaries.


Alternatively I could email you the converted firmware files from my system.


Nick


